I read the instructions given below on the phone screen again.
Very formal language is used there.
The instructions say, "If an SMS does not arrive, a code is sent via email."
I often use this option on government websites.
I tap the "send code by email" button.
Usually I get the code by email quickly.
I open my email app and check the inbox.
The message arrives in my inbox immediately.
I open the email and read the six-digit code.
I go back to the portal.
I type that code in the empty space.
Then I press the 'submit' button.
The screen pauses for a little while.
Then a big green checkmark appears on the screen.
There is another formal message below the green checkmark.
It says, "Your profile has been successfully updated."
I feel very relieved.
Usually, a lot of time is wasted on such small tasks.
But finally this boring task is complete.
Now I turn off my phone.
